<title>INDIA: India PNB cuts prime lending rate to 13.5 pct - UNI.</title>
<headline>India PNB cuts prime lending rate to 13.5 pct - UNI.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Punjab National Bank (PNB) on Saturday announced a cut in its prime lending rate (PLR) by 100 basis points to 13.5 percent from 14.5 percent, the United News of India (UNI) said.</p>
<p>The interest rate does not include interest tax, the news agency said.</p>
<p>PNB's maximum spread on loan advances other than consumer credit will be four percent over the PLR, UNI said.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom, +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
